{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinearIncrementingEntityIdGenerator"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This entity id generator creates linearly incrementing entity ids","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless an entity is marked as unused then the marked id is returned next in a FIFO order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with an increased generation.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The slot index 0 is reserved and never provided; slots start at generation 0. A slot whose generation reaches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32.max"},{"text":" is retired and never provided again.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Furthermore it respects order of entity ids on initialization, meaning the provided ids on initialization will be provided in order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until all are in use. After that the free entities start at the lowest available id increasing linearly skipping already in-use entity ids.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/linearincrementingentityidgenerator"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Linear incrementing entity id generator","type":"text"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Entities","title":"Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity","doc